WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.100
Who's involved?

2
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.875
Developers maintain the kit.

3
00:00:02.875 --> 00:00:08.400
The project owner owns this gate: enabling
the API and granting the viewer role.

4
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:12.875
And the security officer keeps the
role binding and records the two gaps.

5
00:00:12.875 --> 00:00:14.400
The permissions are short.

6
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.550
The project call needs the
viewer role on the project.

7
00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:21.538
The organization call needs the
same role on the organization,

8
00:00:21.538 --> 00:00:23.225
and it's the unverified one.

9
00:00:23.225 --> 00:00:27.430
Grant at the project unless the
settings' scope really is organization,

10
00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:30.424
because a viewer role
granted at the organization

11
00:00:30.424 --> 00:00:33.275
for a project read is more
read scope than needed.

12
00:00:33.275 --> 00:00:35.180
Nothing the reader holds can write.
